    {'id': 'RLA-C14', 'statement': 'The centralizer owner builds the exact linear equations XG-GX=0 in row-major coordinates, obtains their kernel basis and replays every resulting matrix against all supplied generators. Under lawful field elimination this is a complete finite-dimensional common centralizer construction.', 'evidence': [ev('src/exact_field/commutant.rs', 10, 21), ev('src/exact_field/commutant.rs', 35, 111), ev('src/exact_field/commutant.rs', 126, 140)], 'controls': ['RLA-P17'], 'limits': '355 independent finite families; no native execution. Separate phase budgets do not provide the advertised whole-call scalar bound.'},
