    {'id': 'RLA-F07', 'statement': 'The centralizer-basis function and standalone Penrose verifier reset the scalar-operation allowance across phases. A1x1 generator[1] admits6 counted calls with cap4; verifying the1x1 identity inverse admits8 with cap2. These exceed the facade promise of a whole-operation worst-case bound before scalar work.', 'evidence': [ev('src/exact_field/mod.rs', 47, 54), ev('src/exact_field/commutant.rs', 24, 32), ev('src/exact_field/commutant.rs', 85, 140), ev('src/exact_field/elimination.rs', 182, 191), ev('src/exact_field/matrix.rs', 312, 321), ev('src/exact_field/pseudoinverse.rs', 87, 121)], 'controls': ['RLA-P20'], 'limits': 'Exact tiny source-correspondent models, not retained Rust execution. The top-level pseudoinverse constructor has its own conservative aggregate bound and is not refuted by this witness; no time or scalar-bit complexity claim is made.', 'recommended_action': 'Preflight the sum of construction, elimination and replay costs, or pass a remaining budget across phases; document and name per-operation versus per-subcall limits explicitly.'}
